isplay  you still have the exact same camera  nearly identical software with the  samsung ui on top of android just minus  the iris scanner and secure folder  feature and a few minor things you do  lose the stylus but you actually get a  bigger battery than the note so if you  love the note you will love this this is  the equivalent of like a brother as far  as products in samsung's lineup goes  number two is the regular samsung galaxy  s7 not the edge so this is a little bit  of a further drop off and you lose a  couple more features you don't get as  big of a display or as big of a battery  you don't get the edge display features  from the rounded sides of the galaxy s7  edge but the thing is there's almost no  reason to get the regular s7 if you were  on board with the s7 edge other than  maybe you discovered that your hands are  too small to use a big phone suddenly or  you just don't like having a big phone  anymore in that case the galaxy s7 is  gonna do almost all the same things but  for most people you should still do the  s7 edge all right so number three is the  iphone 7 plus so obviously this is now  going a little bit outside the family  but before you go crazy the iphone 7  plus is actually a really top-notch  phone and it keeps up in a lot of the  ways that the note 7 was really good the  note 7 was a great high-end large phone  and iphone 7 plus is another great  high-end large phone you'll still have a  great battery life you still have a  great camera and you'll still have water  resistance too it's not quad hd super  amoled display but it's easily the best  1080p display in any smartphone so it  still looks pretty good and you'll  actually be keeping a lot of the super  high end hardware and performance and  features by picking up a seven plus now  i don't know how many early adopter  super enthusiast note 7 buyers would  drop everything and buy an iphone ios is  obviously very different from android  but this is definitely still a rock  solid choice and the full review is  incoming for that too so number four is  the lg v20 so this is a phone that was  actually competing directly against the  note 7 in a lot of ways for your money  so it should be a very similar  experience so i've talked about it more  in a second video but this is a phone  that's flying under the radar as far as  great high-end big smartphones go and  it's definitely big no doubting that  bigger footprint even than the note 7  itself but when you consider you get  that big removable battery something the  note 7 obviously didn't have expandable  storage a great camera or pair of  cameras like the iphone 7 plus a really  exceptional dac for great audio and that  unique second display up top for  notifications and saving you screen real  estate on the main display there's a lot  going for it it's not water resistant  and obviously lg is packing a very  different set of features on top of  android than samsung is there's no s pen  but no other phone has an s pen so i  think as far as big android phones go  you probably can't really go wrong with  lg v20 to replace a phone that was  competing against so number five is a  bit more of a wild card but it's the  google pixel xl and this probably  couldn't be a much better time for this  phone to come out of the heat of a lot  of people coming out of the note 7. for  the larger of the two phones running  pure stock android 7.1 out the box a lot  of people haven't been paying much  attention to it or giving it much credit  but the pixel xl is shaping up to be a  pretty good big phone replacement now  the caveat is it's not out right now so  depending on when you watch this there  could be a gap between when you order it  and when you get it or not but if you  can get your hands on a google pixel xl  it's shaping up to look like a pretty  good high-end smartphone but you will be  missing some features right off the gate  the pixel isn't water resistant it  doesn't have expandable storage it  doesn't